--- a/patches/README.md
+++ b/patches/README.md
@@ -331,3 +331,4 @@ Reserved:
   0189 adds the Hub over any app and the cover API to the SableOS home (2.0 plan, BB10, owner decision 2026-11-12): `patch_hub_peek` adds `SableHubPeekActivity` (rows by `SableHubPeek`, unit-tested), opened by holding the Recents key (frameworks/base 0326) or Hub, the new first row of the Alt+BlackBerry key menu; `patch_frame_covers` adds `content://org.sableos.launcher.covers` (`SableCoverProvider`, `SableFrameCovers`, unit-tested), where an app sets or clears its own frame's cover (title and line, the caller's own, in memory, hidden while locked, 24-hour lapse), shown ahead of notification and media summaries.
   0190 is the Hub after the JL10 review (owner, 2026-11-12; ideas only, no JLauncher code or art): `patch_hub_keep` adds `SableHubKeep` (unit-tested), so the Hub keeps items until deleted (on the phone only, at most 1000, ongoing notices and Sable Mail not kept), lists Unread then Today, Yesterday and dated sections under "All accounts · N unread", adds Priority Hub and each app with its unread count to Views, a ⋮ menu (Hub settings, Email accounts, Calendar accounts, Connected apps), Mark unread, Priority Hub entries and Delete in the row menu, and Hub settings for Keep messages, Every message on its own, System notifications and the Sable Mail and DAVx⁵ account links; `patch_status_icons` names the home status choices Dials, Icons, Hidden everywhere (the saved value stays `text`); `patch_extra_dim` adds `SableExtraDim` (unit-tested), which turns on Android's Extra dim with manual brightness at the slider's bottom and off when it moves up, leaving Extra dim the person set alone (the Q25 panel's lowest backlight step is still bright); the AppSummary test now counts the cover source as local.
   0191 makes the SableOS home need no permission setup (owner, 2026-11-12): `patch_home_access` adds `SableHomeAccess` (unit-tested), which grants the home Contacts, Calendar, Call log, Photos, Notifications, notification access, usage access and display over other apps once on its first start (each item until granted once, so a later "off" stays off; location is left to the person), and drops the Active Frames page from Launcher settings; product/q25 default permissions grant the same runtime permissions at first boot.
+  0192 slims Active Frames' name bar (owner, 2026-11-12): the bar under each frame is 22 dp with a smaller title and close mark, so more of the app shows; X and Backspace still close a frame. `SableTaskSnapshots` now finds TaskSnapshotManager.getTaskSnapshot by name (an added flag no longer hides it) and logs once under `SableFrames` which snapshot permissions the home holds, so `adb logcat -s SableFrames` says why a frame shows a summary instead of its picture.
